american and haitian authorities are  still working to free 17 members of an  american-based missionary group who were  kidnapped in haiti almost three weeks  ago the leader of the kidnappers has  threatened to kill those hostages unless  a 17 million dollar ransom is paid 1  million dollars for each hostage the  white house says that president biden is  briefed on the situation every single  day  former u.s special envoy to haiti daniel  foote meanwhile resigned back in  september to protest the biden  administration's overall haiti policy in  his first interview since resigning foot  told face the nation moderator margaret  brennan why  i realized the only way i'd get the  right attention was by  going nuclear and resilient ambassador  daniel foote's frustrations with what he  calls the biden administration's deeply  flawed haiti policy were mounting when  did you foresee there were problems with  the biden policy  uh  i would say  late august early september what was it  that made you say i can't do this  first  the  del rio texas  bridge situation with 15 000 haitians  i learned about deportations  by the press like everybody else which  was troubling to me due to the pandemic  migrants who illegally enter the u.s are  being expelled without an asylum hearing  seventeen thousand haitians crossed  between september and october over seven  thousand six hundred were sent back  the  haitian state cannot take care of the  people that it currently has and to put  thousands or tens of thousands of  additional desperate people into that  situation is only going to  fuel a terrible situation  the biden administration disputes foot's  version of events but a second state  department official also resigned to  protest the migration policy  migrants are expected to continue  fleeing due to haiti's deteriorating  security after the july assassination of  president johannel moyes this man  arielle henry stepped in as acting prime  minister do you believe the acting prime  minister played a role in the  assassination of president moyes i  can't answer that there are allegations  there are phone records that indicate  that he had several conversations before  and after the assassination with one of  the prime suspects ariel henry has some  questions to answer for his citizenry  henri denies the allegations the state  department says it supports the current  government but wants haitians to decide  their own fate did you ever  propose any kind of military  intervention to haiti i propose sending  a company or so of us special forces to  train  an anti-gang task force within the  national haitian national police so  you're talking about  30 60 people the biden administration  opposes sending troops but gangs are  gaining ground even cutting off the  country's fuel supply and taking  hostages  a group of christian missionaries  including 16 americans are being held by  the gang called 400 mawozo the gangs are  stronger than the police the police are  out gunned and overmatched right now  they need lethal aid they need training  we can give that to them can america  live with a failed haitian state next  door no  i i mean we can but it's going to have a  major negative impact on us  powerful interview there for margaret  brennan
 

